      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Modeling",
      "items": [
        "Architecture composes scopes, arrays, processors, memory regions, routers, networks, and shared resources.",
        "Symbolic expressions and constraints carry parameterized sizes and costs across the model."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Evaluation and interchange",
      "items": [
        "MLIR describes executable functionality; YAML attaches function-level performance scenarios.",
        "Schedule evaluation resolves in process, while ABI helpers support generated evaluator and query binaries."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Visualization",
      "items": [
        "Rust exporters produce graph, hierarchy, or combined viewer payloads.",
        "The React/Vite frontend validates those payloads and converts them into interactive graph and hierarchy views."
